Claim: It was originally purchased with money wired to CFAR from Sam Bankman-Fried’s company, FTX, as it was collapsing.

## Your earlier research
The claim is misleading. It says the property (Lighthaven, the former Rose Garden Inn in Berkeley) was originally bought with money wired from FTX to CFAR as FTX was collapsing. The evidence doesn't support that.

What the evidence shows:
- The FTX estate's complaint alleged two $500K payments (July and August 2022) from the FTX Foundation to a title company as a deposit on the purchase. The same complaint calls these a loan that was never repaid, and says a 'material portion' of other transfers to CFAR was used for the purchase and renovation. These are allegations, not findings. https://forum.effectivealtruism.org/posts/YSuqwrXFtuXuSzGDc/linkpost-sam-bankman-fried-funded-a-group-with-racist-ties
- The deposits were wired in July and August 2022. The sale closed around November 4, 2022, which is about when FTX collapsed. They were not wired during the collapse.
- The deposits went to a title/escrow company, not to CFAR. Lightcone's Oliver Habryka says no FTX funds were used to buy Lighthaven. He says the escrow company was trying to return the $1M, and he posted a 2022 escrow document saying the $1M would go back to an FTX-linked company. https://www.sfgate.com/tech/article/sbf-berkeley-rose-garden-inn-19520351.php and https://protos.com/ftx-chasing-5m-spent-on-right-wing-conference-venue/
- The purchase was financed mainly by a roughly $16.5M loan from Jaan Tallinn. https://forum.effectivealtruism.org/posts/rsnrpvKofps5Py7di/shutting-down-the-lightcone-offices and https://hoodline.com/2026/09/inside-berkeley-s-lighthaven-where-ai-doomers-gather-to-debate-the-end-of-the-world/
- Lightcone later settled with the FTX estate, paying $1.7M with help from Tallinn and SFC. It says FTX never gave money directly for Lighthaven. https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/5n2ZQcbc7r4R8mvqc/the-lightcone-is-nothing-without-its-people-lw-lighthaven-s-5
- Vox's Kelsey Piper called the Guardian's claim that FTX funds bought Lighthaven a serious error. https://forum.effectivealtruism.org/posts/YSuqwrXFtuXuSzGDc/linkpost-sam-bankman-fried-funded-a-group-with-racist-ties

The claim therefore states a contested allegation as settled fact. It overstates FTX's role in funding the purchase and is imprecise about when and where the money went.

